body:
@vicb I think you are right.

https://github.com/angular/angular/blob/master/packages/core/src/change_detection/differs/default_iterable_differ.ts#L196

On the third item check, I took a screen shot before and after it calls `_verifyReinsertion`. It looks like the record it is returning is also being used to progress to the next record, which in this case, is causing the record to show it being added and then deleted.

Before:
<img width="649" alt="before-verifyreinsertion" src="https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/8039397/27719388-16f8be9e-5d20-11e7-8399-1021d78faec0.png">

After:
<img width="644" alt="after-verifyreinsertion" src="https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/8039397/27719391-1ae94a64-5d20-11e7-9f0d-d9f992ef8962.png">

Could the fix be as simple as the following?
```
// Create a temp variable so as to not affect the next record in the loop
let checkRecord = record;
if (mayBeDirty) {
    // TODO(misko): can we limit this to duplicates only?
    checkRecord = this._verifyReinsertion(checkRecord, item, itemTrackBy, index);
}
if (!looseIdentical(checkRecord.item, item)) this._addIdentityChange(checkRecord, item);
```
so record is not changed for when it calls `record = record._next;`.
